meta {
  name: Get Agency Profile
  type: http
  seq: 16
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/agency/profile
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{ownerAccessToken}}
}

tests {
  test("returns 200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("reports the agency name and an IANA time zone", function () {
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect(body.agencyName).to.be.a("string").and.not.be.empty;
    expect(body.timezone).to.match(/^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_+-]*(\/[A-Za-z0-9_+-]+)*$/);
  });
}

docs {
  # GET /agency/profile — the agency's own time zone (PAC-141)

  The owner-editable facts about the agency itself. Today that is one field,
  the IANA zone the agency keeps its working day in.

  - **Module:** none (`@SkipModule()`) — the agency's identity is not a
    product module that can be switched off.
  - **Permission:** `agency:branding:read` — reused rather than minted, for the
    reason `GET /agency/setup` gives: the vocabulary is a fixed contract and a
    new `agency:profile:*` pair would reach existing owners only after
    `api:sync:roles` on every environment. By default only the Agency Owner
    holds it.
  - **Data scope:** none — the caller's own agency, from the token.

  ## What the zone drives
  - Every dashboard date window — `today`, `week`, `mtd`, the Owner view's
    presets, the Manager view's business-day aging, the leaderboard's default
    month — is cut on this calendar (`AccessContext.timeZone`, resolved once per
    request).
  - The 8 PM end-of-day Away sweep (`Set My Availability` → `Agency.timezone`).
  - The calendar day an app-written quote recap is filed on.

  ## Response `200`
  ```json
  { "agencyName": "Smith Family Agency", "timezone": "America/Chicago" }
  ```

  Defaults to `America/Chicago` (US Central) for every agency that has never
  set one; the Super Admin onboarding wizard pre-selects the same.

  ## Errors
  - `403` — caller lacks `agency:branding:read`.
}
